# Representative sample - illustrates the %SEC-6-IPACCESSLOGP message
# format Cisco IOS emits for a logged ACL deny match. This project's
# actual GUEST-CONTAINMENT ACL (01-regional-on-premises-network/switching/
# MY-KL-HQ-CORE.cfg) does not currently have the `log` keyword appended to
# its deny lines, so these exact lines were never emitted by a live
# device - they're reconstructed in the real Cisco syslog format, using
# this project's own real addressing (GUEST_WIFI 10.10.30.0/24 attempting
# to reach MGMT 10.10.10.0/24 and DMZ_SERVERS 10.10.40.0/24), to
# demonstrate what Wazuh would actually ingest and alert on if logging
# were enabled on this ACL.
